#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# coefficient_list

#% text
# `coefficient_list(p, x)` gives the list of the coefficients of `x^0`, `x^1`, ..., `x^degree(p, x)` in the polynomial `p`.

#% text
# `coefficient_list(p, [x, y, ...])` gives the nested lists for several variables.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `p` is expanded first; missing powers have coefficient 0. The zero polynomial gives `[]`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
coefficient_list(x^3 - 2*x + 5, x)
#% output
#= [5, -2, 0, 1]

#% cell
coefficient_list((1 + x)^4, x)
#% output
#= [1, 4, 6, 4, 1]

#% cell
coefficient_list(a*x^2 + b, x)
#% output
#= [b, 0, a]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Two variables, with the first variable's powers outermost:

#% cell
coefficient_list(1 + x + x*y + y^2, [x, y])
#% output
#= [[1, 0, 1], [1, 1, 0]]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The coefficients rebuild the polynomial:

#% cell
p = 3*x^3 - x + 7; c = coefficient_list(p, x); sum(c[k + 1]*x^k, [k, 0, 3]) == p
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `coefficient`, `degree`, `expand`
